## Examples (MOST IMPORTANT)
- examples/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py
  - Shows usage of ArxivToolkit with ChatAgent
  - Demonstrates searching and downloading papers with Arxiv tools
  - Uses ModelFactory to create default model and ChatAgent with Arxiv tools

- examples/rag/single_agent_with_hybrid_rag.py
  - Shows example of single agent using HybridRetriever for retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)
  - Demonstrates querying with vector retrieval and answering questions

## Implementation
- camel/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py
  - Class: ArxivToolkit
  - Implements arXiv API interaction: search_papers, download_papers
  - Provides tools for searching and downloading papers

- camel/memories/blocks/vectordb_block.py
  - Class: VectorDBBlock
  - Implements vector database memory block using embeddings and vector storage
  - Supports retrieve and write_records for vector-based memory

- camel/agents/chat_agent.py
  - Class: ChatAgent
  - Core agent class managing conversation, tools, memory, and model interaction
  - Supports tool calling, memory management, summarization, and streaming

## Enums (for exact values)
- camel/types/enums.py
  - ModelPlatformType: DEFAULT, OPENAI, TOGETHER, etc.
  - ModelType: DEFAULT, GPT_4, GPT_3_5_TURBO, etc.
  - RoleType: ASSISTANT, USER, SYSTEM
  - OpenAIBackendRole: ASSISTANT, SYSTEM, FUNCTION, TOOL

These files and classes provide the necessary components to create an agent with Arxiv tools, download papers, and use vector retrieval to answer questions. The example in `examples/toolkits/arxiv_toolkit.py` is especially relevant as it shows how to use ArxivToolkit with ChatAgent. The vector retrieval memory block is implemented in `camel/memories/blocks/vectordb_block.py`. The core agent functionality is in `camel/agents/chat_agent.py`. The enums in `camel/types/enums.py` help configure model and platform types.
